  "id": "DrugBank_DB08826 - MONDO_11381",
  "verbalization": "Deferiprone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Dominant Beta-thalassemia through its association with Beta-thalassemia Hbb/lcrb and Beta-thalassemia Intermedia, both of which are subtypes of the disease. These subtypes are linked to the overproduction of beta-globin, leading to hemolysis and anemia. Deferiprone's indication for Beta-thalassemia Hbb/lcrb and Intermedia suggests a potential role in modulating the disease process, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is supported by the shared indication with Luspatercept, a drug that targets the same pathway, and by the indication of Deferasirox, another agent that interacts with the same disease subtypes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism involving the regulation of beta-globin synthesis, though the precise molecular interactions and therapeutic implications require further investigation.",
